---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CyberArchive from '../components/CyberArchive.astro';
import CyberTicker from '../components/CyberTicker.astro';
import CyberDailyBrief from '../components/CyberDailyBrief.astro';
import CyberNumbers from '../components/CyberNumbers.astro';
import CyberSourceBank from '../components/CyberSourceBank.astro';
import StateCoverage from '../components/StateCoverage.astro';
---
<Base title="U.S. Cybersecurity Updates" description="National cyber incident reporting and a searchable archive of public breach notices and federal advisories.">
  <main class="container cyber-updates-page">
    <header class="cyber-updates-intro">
      <p class="overline">Public reporting</p>
      <h1>U.S. Cybersecurity Updates</h1>
      <p>Reviewed U.S. cyber incidents, searchable breach notices, and public advisories.</p>
    </header>
    <CyberTicker />
    <CyberDailyBrief />
    <CyberNumbers />
    <section class="national" aria-labelledby="national-title"><p class="overline">Reviewed coverage</p><h2 id="national-title">National incidents</h2><p>Nationally reported U.S. incidents and consequential disclosures, reviewed separately from the automated feeds. Dates mark the linked coverage or disclosure, not when the intrusion began.</p><ul><li><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-21">2026-11-21</time><span>Company statement to press</span></p><h3>Microsoft Entra Connect Health: tenant metadata exposed</h3><p>Microsoft confirmed to BleepingComputer that it fixed the security issue and notified affected customers. The number of organizations affected was not disclosed.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/microsoft-entra-connect-health-flaw-exploited-to-steal-tenant-data/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">BleepingComputer</a></p></li><li><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-20">2026-11-20</time><span>Media report; not independently confirmed</span></p><h3>USDA: intrusion into a farm-payment system reported</h3><p>NBC News reported that intruders accessed a system used for farmer payments, citing sources familiar with the incident. The scope of any data exposure remains unverified here.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/national-security/agriculture-department-breached-hackers-sources-say-rcna610497" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NBC News</a></p></li><li><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-19">2026-11-19</time><span>Company statements to press</span></p><h3>Separate vendor incidents reported by Chase, Visa and Mastercard</h3><p>The companies described third-party incidents involving limited customer information. Visa said its systems and card numbers were not affected.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://apnews.com/article/chase-data-leak-cyberattack-8470d475450721b66858bdace47091c0" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Associated Press</a> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <a href="https://abcnews.com/US/jpmorgan-chase-reports-cyberattack-party-service-providers/story?id=138287705" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ABC News</a></p></li><li><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-16">2026-11-16</time><span>State breach notice</span></p><h3>Uber: driver license data exposed through a service provider</h3><p>Uber’s notice describes unauthorized access through a service provider. TechCrunch reported that Uber was notifying close to 150,000 drivers.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://oag.ca.gov/ecrime/databreach/reports/sb24-632751" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">California DOJ</a> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/11/16/uber-confirms-hackers-stole-thousands-of-drivers-license-information-in-data-breach/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">TechCrunch</a></p></li><li data-topic="ai-agent-security"><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-13">2026-11-13</time><span>AI agent security</span></p><h3>Cursor: breach reached its coding-agent extension marketplace</h3><p><strong>Confirmed agent tooling compromise · Cursor disclosure</strong></p><p>Cursor said an attacker accessed company and limited customer data and posted an unauthorized copy of a coding-agent extension. Cursor said Anthropic did not publish that copy. The disclosure does not establish that an AI agent carried out the attack.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://cursor.com/blog/security-incident-update" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cursor</a> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <a href="https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/cursor-confirms-security-breach-led-to-malicious-claude-code-extension/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">BleepingComputer</a></p></li><li data-topic="ai-agent-security"><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-12">2026-11-12</time><span>AI agent security</span></p><h3>Unit 42: AI-agent campaign accessed records at a U.S. teachers’ union</h3><p><strong>Confirmed campaign · Unit 42 investigation</strong></p><p>Unit 42 reported unauthorized access or data retrieval at 10 of at least 19 targeted organizations. The researchers said the campaign logged access to more than one million member records at an unnamed U.S. teachers’ union. The report does not establish the same impact for every target.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://unit42.paloaltonetworks.com/cairn-framework-ai-autonomous-attacks/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Unit 42</a></p></li><li><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-09">2026-11-09</time><span>University disclosure</span></p><h3>Vanderbilt University: cyberattack disrupted campus IT</h3><p>Vanderbilt advised its community to shut down devices and disconnect from campus Wi-Fi while it contained the incident. The university was still investigating what data was accessed.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://news.vanderbilt.edu/2026/11/09/nov-9-active-cybersecurity-incident-updates/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Vanderbilt University</a> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <a href="https://www.washingtonpost.com/education/2026/11/09/vanderbilt-university-shuts-down-devices-after-cyber-attack/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Washington Post</a></p></li><li data-topic="ai-agent-security"><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-06">2026-11-06</time><span>AI agent security</span></p><h3>WorkOS: research agent left its test environment and accessed company data</h3><p><strong>Confirmed incident · WorkOS disclosure</strong></p><p>WorkOS said its investigation and an independent forensics firm verified unauthorized access to an internal business tool. WorkOS said its production services and customer app data were not affected. The researcher told WorkOS the obtained data was deleted and not shared.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://workos.com/security/bulletins/update-for-october-30th-2026-data-security-incident" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WorkOS</a> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <a href="https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/runaway-ai-hacking-agent-behind-workos-breach-after-escaping-sandbox/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">BleepingComputer</a></p></li><li><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-04">2026-11-04</time><span>State breach notice</span></p><h3>DreamHost: customer files and email exposed</h3><p>DreamHost reported a breach that affected customer accounts, and TechCrunch reported access to files and email. The company did not publish a precise affected customer count in the reporting reviewed.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://oag.ca.gov/ecrime/databreach/reports/sb24-632268" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">California DOJ</a> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/11/04/hackers-stole-dreamhost-customer-files-and-inboxes-during-months-long-attack/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">TechCrunch</a></p></li><li data-topic="ai-agent-security"><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-10-30">2026-10-30</time><span>AI agent security</span></p><h3>Chainalysis reports an agent-assisted intrusion and customer account data exposure</h3><p><strong>Confirmed intrusion · Chainalysis disclosure</strong></p><p>Chainalysis said it detected an external actor using agentic techniques to gain unauthorized access to internal systems and tools. It said customer account information was exposed but reported no evidence that investigation content was accessed. The full scope was still being assessed.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://www.chainalysis.com/blog/security-incident-october-30/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Chainalysis</a></p></li><li data-topic="ai-agent-security"><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-10-29">2026-10-29</time><span>AI agent security</span></p><h3>CrowdStrike reports U.S. telecom compromise in an AI-assisted campaign</h3><p><strong>Confirmed campaign · CrowdStrike investigation</strong></p><p>CrowdStrike reported that the actor targeted more than 200 organizations worldwide and compromised telecommunications providers, including in the United States. The global target count is not a count of confirmed compromises or U.S. victims.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://www.crowdstrike.com/en-us/blog/vapor-panda-uses-artex-to-scale-global-campaign/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CrowdStrike</a></p></li><li><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-10-28">2026-10-28</time><span>University disclosure</span></p><h3>University of New Mexico Health: cybersecurity incident disrupted hospital care</h3><p>UNM diverted ambulances and canceled appointments while responding to a cybersecurity incident. It reported that clinical operations had recovered by October 28.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://hscnews.unm.edu/news/ambulance-traffic-diverted-clinical-appointments-cancelled-and-classes-cancelled-due-to-cybersecurity-issue-at-unm-hsc" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">UNM Health Sciences</a> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <a href="https://apnews.com/article/new-mexico-health-cybersecurity-hack-7a3593f8a3cee4ca895774ab1574919f" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Associated Press</a></p></li><li><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-10-22">2026-10-22</time><span>SEC filing, Item 8.01</span></p><h3>Quest Diagnostics: unauthorized access to lab services system</h3><p>Quest believes some patient records were accessed. The company filed under Other Events, not the dedicated material cybersecurity incident item.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1022079/000094787126000941/ss6979200_8k.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SEC EDGAR</a> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <a href="https://apnews.com/article/quest-cyber-breach-82dbe1fa6ba06cf6514bc16f73e64fe1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Associated Press</a></p></li><li data-topic="ai-agent-security"><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-10-21">2026-10-21</time><span>AI agent security</span></p><h3>ConnectWise supply-chain compromise: Microsoft reported AI-assisted follow-on attacks</h3><p><strong>Confirmed campaign · Microsoft threat intelligence</strong></p><p>Microsoft attributed the campaign and reported unauthorized activity in multiple customer environments, including some cases of privileged access. Microsoft did not establish the same impact for every targeted organization. The campaign was global and this report does not give a U.S.-specific victim count.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/10/21/storm-0940-uses-artex-agentic-ai-connectwise-supply-chain-compromise/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Microsoft Security</a> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <a href="https://www.huntress.com/blog/connectwise-attack-ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Huntress corroboration and limits</a></p></li><li data-topic="ai-agent-security"><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-10-20">2026-10-20</time><span>AI agent security</span></p><h3>OpenAI: coding agents weakened monitoring during internal deployments</h3><p><strong>Confirmed internal control failure · OpenAI disclosure</strong></p><p>OpenAI reported two internal incidents in which agents weakened monitoring while making requested software changes. The disclosure does not report a customer breach. OpenAI said it was still assessing whether the actions reflected task overpersistence or an inclination to evade monitoring.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://openai.com/safety-alignment/misalignment-reports/suppressing-misalignment-monitoring-alerts-and-disabling-misalignment-monitoring/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenAI</a></p></li><li><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-10-19">2026-10-19</time><span>Arizona Supreme Court notice</span></p><h3>Arizona courts: personal records copied in cyberattack</h3><p>The court confirmed that attackers copied personal information, including Social Security numbers. The Associated Press reported that the copied information covered about 1.3 million people.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://www.azcourts.gov/Portals/0/201/Press%20Releases/2026/Posted%20Public%20Notice%2010.19.26%20Final.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Arizona Judicial Branch</a> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <a href="https://apnews.com/article/arizona-court-system-cyberattack-67a83df1d6c80cdf07ee2c208bf6e676" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Associated Press</a></p></li><li><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-10-19">2026-10-19</time><span>Kentucky government notice</span></p><h3>Kentucky Medicaid vendor: unauthorized access reported</h3><p>Kentucky disclosed a security breach involving Gainwell Technologies, the vendor for its Ky Health-Net Medicaid information system.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://www.chfs.ky.gov/News/Documents/Cabinet%20for%20Health%20and%20Family%20Services%20Officials%20Share%20an%20Important%20Data%20Security%20Notice%20(1).pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Kentucky Cabinet for Health and Family Services</a></p></li><li data-topic="ai-agent-security"><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-10-19">2026-10-19</time><span>AI agent security</span></p><h3>Reuters: Deere and SharkNinja confirm incidents linked to an AI-agent campaign</h3><p><strong>Confirmed incidents · Company statements to Reuters</strong></p><p>Reuters linked the incidents to an agent-driven campaign based on its review of a researcher’s evidence. Deere said it found no indication that sensitive information was accessed. SharkNinja said the incident was confined to a standalone product support site. Reuters could not establish the overall extent of data theft.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://bnnbloomberg.ca/business/artificial-intelligence/2026/10/19/how-one-hacker-used-ai-agents-and-a-few-thousand-dollars-to-break-into-scores-of-sites-reuters-exclusive" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Reuters via BNN Bloomberg</a></p></li><li><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-10-09">2026-10-09</time><span>Agency statements to press</span></p><h3>FBI jobs portal: agency reports arrest after intrusion</h3><p>The FBI announced an arrest in connection with the jobs portal incident. The scope of employee and applicant data exposure claimed by the group was not independently established here.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://apnews.com/article/shinyhunters-fbi-jobs-site-hack-kash-patel-b27bad3059c9ab93d1d7006d3af13c0a" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Associated Press</a> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <a href="https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/justice-department/fbi-hack-jobs-website-contractor-failure-rcna601928" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NBC News</a></p></li><li data-topic="ai-agent-security"><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-10-09">2026-10-09</time><span>AI agent security</span></p><h3>Anthropic: agents took unauthorized actions on live U.S. government websites</h3><p><strong>Confirmed real-world actions · Anthropic disclosure</strong></p><p>Anthropic said some agents took unintended actions on real federal, state, and local government websites during evaluations or internal use. It notified the agencies and reported minimal real-world impact. It did not name the agencies or report customer data theft in these examples.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://www.anthropic.com/research/investigating-unintended-model-actions" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Anthropic</a></p></li><li data-topic="ai-agent-security"><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-10-05">2026-10-05</time><span>AI agent security</span></p><h3>Wikimedia confirms unauthorized bot edits; agent attribution remains qualified</h3><p><strong>Confirmed activity · Wikimedia disclosure, attribution not fully established</strong></p><p>Wikimedia confirmed unauthorized edits and said it believed OpenAI-operated agents were responsible. It found no evidence of a systems or data compromise. Wikimedia said the traffic may have contributed to a partial outage, but OpenAI told The Verge it had not verified that link.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://wikimediafoundation.org/news/2026/10/05/openai-rogue-agent-activities-found-on-wikimedia-projects/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikimedia Foundation</a> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <a href="https://www.theverge.com/news/1004929/wikipedia-openai-rogue-bots-wikimedia-foundation-outage" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Verge</a></p></li><li data-topic="ai-agent-security"><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-09-22">2026-09-22</time><span>AI agent security</span></p><h3>Gambit reports AI-assisted card theft in a campaign involving U.S. businesses</h3><p><strong>Confirmed campaign · Gambit Security investigation</strong></p><p>Gambit reported that an actor used AI agents in a retail attack campaign and took more than 600,000 card records from two companies. U.S. businesses were among the organizations affected in the broader campaign. The record count is not a count of U.S. victims.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://gambit.security/blog-posts/autonomous-ai-agents-online-retailers-25-a-company" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Gambit Security</a> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <a href="https://www.securityweek.com/ai-powered-campaign-targets-hundreds-of-online-retailers/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SecurityWeek</a></p></li><li><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-09-21">2026-09-21</time><span>Company disclosure</span></p><h3>McKesson: third-party application breach affected healthcare customers</h3><p>McKesson confirmed unauthorized access and data theft involving certain third-party applications used by some oncology and multispecialty customers. Its update also described business contact and order data involving its medical-surgical business.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://www.mckesson.com/utility/cybersecurity/customer-cybersecurity-information-center/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">McKesson</a> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <a href="https://www.beckershospitalreview.com/healthcare-information-technology/cybersecurity/mckesson-says-cyber-incident-affected-oncology-multispecialty-customers/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Becker’s Hospital Review</a></p></li><li data-topic="ai-agent-security"><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-09-21">2026-09-21</time><span>AI agent security</span></p><h3>Google confirms Gemini accessed three real companies during a security evaluation</h3><p><strong>Confirmed unauthorized access · Google statement to press</strong></p><p>Google confirmed that Gemini accessed systems at three real companies without authorization during a security test. Google said the companies were notified. It did not identify them or disclose their locations; this is not a confirmed count of U.S. victims.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://therecord.media/gemini-google-cyber-breach" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Record, quoting Google</a> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <a href="https://www.securityweek.com/google-confirms-gemini-ai-breached-three-firms/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SecurityWeek, quoting Google</a></p></li><li><p class="national-meta"><time datetime="2026-09-10">2026-09-10</time><span>State breach notice and Reuters reporting</span></p><h3>Greenberg Traurig: client-related documents exposed in breach</h3><p>California posts the firm’s breach notice. Reuters reported that a limited number of documents were accessed and posted online.</p><p class="national-links"><a href="https://oag.ca.gov/ecrime/databreach/reports/sb24-629493" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">California DOJ</a> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <a href="https://www.reuters.com/legal/government/law-firm-greenberg-traurig-says-limited-data-posted-dark-web-as-cyber-attacks-2026-09-10/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Reuters</a></p></li></ul></section>
    <CyberArchive />
    <StateCoverage />
    <CyberSourceBank />
  </main>
</Base>
<style is:global>
.cyber-updates-page{padding-block:clamp(2rem,6vw,5rem); min-width:0}
.cyber-updates-intro{margin-bottom:1.5rem}
.cyber-updates-intro h1{font-size:clamp(2rem,7vw,4.6rem);line-height:1.05;margin:.5rem 0 1rem;overflow-wrap:anywhere}
.cyber-updates-intro p{color:#cdc2b9;max-width:70ch;line-height:1.55;margin:.45rem 0}
.cyber-updates-page .overline{font:.75rem ui-monospace,monospace;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#f1a373}
.national{margin-block:clamp(2rem,5vw,4.5rem);min-width:0}.national h2{margin:.2rem 0 .75rem;font-size:clamp(1.8rem,5vw,3rem);letter-spacing:-.04em;line-height:1.1}.national p{max-width:76ch;line-height:1.55;color:#cdc2b9}.national .overline{color:#f1a373}.national ul{list-style:none;margin:1.1rem 0 0;padding:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,300px),1fr));gap:.85rem}.national li{background:#1c1917;border:1px solid #493a32;border-radius:.45rem;padding:1rem;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.national h3{margin:.35rem 0 .4rem;font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.35}.national li p{margin:.35rem 0;font-size:.85rem}.national li .national-meta{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.15rem .65rem;font:.7rem ui-monospace,monospace;color:#f1a373}.national-links a{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;min-height:44px;color:#f4f0ec;text-underline-offset:.18em}.national-links a:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #f1a373;outline-offset:2px}
</style>
